WEBVTT

00:11.327 --> 00:15.667
<i>Long ago, scholars used geometry
 to learn the size and scope</i>

00:16.007 --> 00:18.567
<i>of the Earth for the first time.</i>

00:20.227 --> 00:24.037
<i>In which case, is it also possible 
to use geometry to determine</i>

00:24.037 --> 00:26.707
<i>the size and scope of the fate
 we hold in our hands?</i>

00:28.607 --> 00:35.137
<i>This is the story of a witch
who made a vast continent her plaything.</i>

01:37.727 --> 01:43.747
<b>Jaadugar</b>

01:48.597 --> 01:52.127
And just where are you trying
 to fly to, my little bird?

01:54.287 --> 01:56.267
You are such a handful, child.

01:59.017 --> 02:02.417
<b>A.D. 1213
Tus
Eastern Iran</b>

02:01.167 --> 02:04.667
<b>Tus</b>

02:05.247 --> 02:10.717
<b>All That Is in the Heavens and All That Is in the Earth</b>

02:31.517 --> 02:34.957
I love how full of life the bazaar is.

02:35.307 --> 02:36.647
Mistress.

02:36.647 --> 02:39.807
When your iddah mourning period for 
the late master ends, let's come shopping.

02:39.807 --> 02:40.957
Good idea.

02:41.487 --> 02:46.397
For today, though, I hope Allah
will lead us to a fine slave.

02:46.397 --> 02:48.027
Not as fine as you, of course.

02:56.137 --> 02:58.327
All of them are hard workers.

02:59.537 --> 03:03.297
This woman, for example,
is skilled at cooking.

03:03.297 --> 03:05.017
This one is a skilled seamstress.

03:05.017 --> 03:06.487
And this one's a talker,

03:06.487 --> 03:10.127
so perhaps she'd make a good conversation
 partner for you, Lady Fatima.

03:10.127 --> 03:11.657
Perhaps.

03:11.657 --> 03:13.887
But what we most need 
help with right now is...

03:13.887 --> 03:17.597
The cleaning. That huge mansion 
is too much for me to handle alone.

03:17.957 --> 03:22.107
Yes, and I still haven't finished sorting
through my late husband's belongings.

03:22.107 --> 03:23.437
Ah, say no more.

03:23.437 --> 03:25.707
Then, how about this woman?

03:25.707 --> 03:27.927
She has a true gift for cleaning.

03:28.507 --> 03:30.327
My name is Anis.

03:30.327 --> 03:32.807
Cleaning isn't about 
what you wish to discard,

03:32.807 --> 03:34.067
but what you wish to keep.

03:34.657 --> 03:37.637
Your days will be neat and tidy.
I give you my word.

03:37.637 --> 03:39.217
That would be wonderful.

03:39.217 --> 03:40.117
How much for her?

03:41.197 --> 03:43.647
I'll let you have her for 800 dirham.

03:44.327 --> 03:46.747
I know slaves aren't cheap,
but my goodness...

03:46.987 --> 03:50.337
Mr. Ahmad, please.
Can't you go a little lower?

03:52.187 --> 03:54.827
I would normally refuse,

03:55.337 --> 03:59.217
but I <i>could</i> make an exception
and let you have her for half price.

03:59.217 --> 04:00.147
What?

03:59.217 --> 04:00.147
What?

04:00.147 --> 04:01.657
But in return...

04:02.197 --> 04:03.077
Come.

04:12.527 --> 04:14.357
Go on. Do as I taught you.

04:16.067 --> 04:17.577
Oh, how cute.

04:17.577 --> 04:18.527
Who's this?

04:18.527 --> 04:21.497
I acquired her just the other day.
Her name is Sitara.

04:21.497 --> 04:24.867
Oh, your name means "star." How lovely.

04:28.877 --> 04:33.937
She's a bit bashful, but as you can see,
her smile is quite fetching.

04:33.937 --> 04:39.257
If properly educated, I reckon she could
be a servant to someone of high standing.

04:39.597 --> 04:41.347
So here's my proposal.

04:41.347 --> 04:42.807
Lady Fatima.

04:42.807 --> 04:45.457
Yours is a scholarly household,

04:45.457 --> 04:50.067
and Young Master Muhammad's keen mind
shines brightly even here in Tus.

04:50.067 --> 04:52.577
Studying in your home 
will give her real cachet.

04:52.577 --> 04:55.777
So might I trouble you 
to take her in for a while?

05:03.717 --> 05:05.787
You agreed to his deal?

05:06.467 --> 05:11.137
Please. You're the only one qualified
 to be her teacher now, Brother.

05:11.137 --> 05:14.757
I'm still in my iddah, and I don't know
any teachers outside our family.

05:15.207 --> 05:21.057
Besides, slave or no, seeking knowledge
 is the duty of every Muslim.

05:22.017 --> 05:23.637
I suppose.

05:25.507 --> 05:28.097
Recitation is the cornerstone 
of all learning.

05:28.097 --> 05:31.437
The first step on that journey
is to recite the Quran properly.

05:31.667 --> 05:33.917
Now, repeat after me.

05:34.997 --> 05:39.867
"In the name of Allah,
the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful."

05:43.307 --> 05:44.287
Now you.

05:46.327 --> 05:48.287
Go on. Try saying it.

05:52.137 --> 05:55.107
It's hopeless. This girl 
has absolutely no talent.

05:55.107 --> 05:58.777
Try as I might, she just smiles
and shows no interest in learning.

05:58.777 --> 06:01.007
But I promised I would take her in.

06:02.537 --> 06:05.637
I'll pay back the discount
you got on the other slave.

06:05.637 --> 06:07.597
I'm sorry, Brother.

06:10.747 --> 06:14.147
I'll have him come fetch you.
Wait here a while, all right?

06:14.647 --> 06:17.567
Mr. Ahmad's establishment, right? I'll go.

06:17.567 --> 06:19.607
Yes. Sorry to trouble you.

06:24.957 --> 06:25.927
<i>I have to get away.</i>

06:27.877 --> 06:32.027
<i>I don't wanna get sold off 
to who knows where. I'm going home.</i>

07:05.567 --> 07:06.927
<i>I'm lost.</i>

07:06.927 --> 07:08.537
<i>Where's the way out?</i>

07:15.337 --> 07:16.767
<i>A boy?</i>

07:25.517 --> 07:30.727
And Young Master Muhammad's keen mind
shines brightly even here in Tus.

07:33.937 --> 07:35.477
Excuse me.

07:35.777 --> 07:36.727
Where's the door?

07:37.267 --> 07:39.027
Th-This is most improper.

07:39.507 --> 07:42.677
A female mustn't show herself before a man
with her hair uncovered.

07:43.577 --> 07:46.017
It's okay. I'm still little.

07:46.017 --> 07:47.267
You're too close.

07:47.267 --> 07:49.947
Besides, you look like 
you're still a child to me,

07:49.947 --> 07:51.567
Young Master Muhammad.

07:51.567 --> 07:53.667
Who are you, anyway?

07:54.557 --> 07:55.257
My name is—

07:55.257 --> 07:56.797
Ah! <i>There</i> you are!

07:56.797 --> 07:59.127
I've looked high and low
after you ran off.

08:00.267 --> 08:02.407
The roses were so pretty,
I had to come look.

08:02.407 --> 08:04.377
She was looking for the way out.

08:07.347 --> 08:10.327
Unbelievable. How could you try to escape?

08:10.327 --> 08:15.377
Now, now. My brother will be back
with Ahmad any minute now.

08:15.377 --> 08:16.307
I'm so sorry.

08:16.307 --> 08:17.957
You wanted to go back, didn't you?

08:20.017 --> 08:22.277
Not to that man's place.

08:22.867 --> 08:25.247
To the house I lived in with my mother.

08:26.037 --> 08:29.987
My mother died, 
and her master sold me off.

08:29.987 --> 08:32.617
Then it's not your house.

08:32.617 --> 08:34.327
You're a slave.

08:34.327 --> 08:36.037
If you want a <i>real</i> home to return to,

08:36.037 --> 08:38.887
study hard so you'll be bought
 by a good master.

08:38.887 --> 08:40.957
Then, I'm never <i>ever</i> gonna study!

08:41.227 --> 08:44.347
I don't wanna study!
I won't make cute faces anymore, either!

08:44.347 --> 08:45.967
It only makes me more valuable!

08:45.967 --> 08:50.257
If I study, I'll get sold off again 
somewhere even farther away than this!

08:50.607 --> 08:53.567
I'm sick of going places
where I don't recognize anything!

08:56.337 --> 08:58.877
Little girl. Your name is Sitara?

08:58.877 --> 09:01.447
So that's the reason
you came here to study?

09:02.537 --> 09:05.287
Our lots in life might be
rather different, and yet...

09:05.927 --> 09:06.907
Say, Zumurrud.

09:07.527 --> 09:10.207
Would you fetch me a water bucket
 from the kitchen?

09:10.617 --> 09:12.057
The larger the better.

09:12.057 --> 09:13.347
Of course.

09:14.137 --> 09:15.087
Come with me.

09:18.047 --> 09:19.707
Where are we going?

09:24.107 --> 09:25.307
The roof?

09:32.597 --> 09:34.427
Will this do?

09:34.427 --> 09:36.167
Yes, thank you.

09:38.557 --> 09:40.937
I'm going to drop this
into the courtyard, okay?

09:47.457 --> 09:48.447
Young Master?

09:48.447 --> 09:50.897
Is that girl really a lost cause?

09:52.767 --> 09:55.557
Wh-What was that? What's going on?

10:01.927 --> 10:04.677
What was that noise just now?
 Is everyone all right?

10:04.677 --> 10:06.667
Did lightning strike the house?

10:06.667 --> 10:09.007
A-Are you sure we aren't
under enemy attack?

10:09.007 --> 10:10.877
Is it those barbarous nomads?

10:14.537 --> 10:15.907
A water bucket?

10:16.277 --> 10:17.727
They're all in a panic.

10:17.727 --> 10:20.187
Young Master, 
your little prank went too far.

10:20.187 --> 10:23.897
If I might ask, why are you two
so calm and composed?

10:24.177 --> 10:25.607
Well, why wouldn't we be?

10:26.127 --> 10:29.527
We knew it was going to hit the ground,
so we covered our ears.

10:32.387 --> 10:37.017
So one might say you predicted a future
in which there would be a loud noise

10:37.017 --> 10:39.787
and took appropriate precautions.
Is that correct?

10:39.787 --> 10:42.417
Well, uh, yes, I suppose.

10:43.297 --> 10:47.047
Perhaps that is what learning
 is all about.

10:48.397 --> 10:51.457
At this moment in time, 
you don't know where you are,

10:51.457 --> 10:53.107
what is happening,

10:53.107 --> 10:55.297
or what is going to become of you.

10:55.297 --> 10:56.887
Your life is full of unknowns.

10:57.347 --> 11:00.407
In a way, my uncle and the others
 down there are the same.

11:01.057 --> 11:03.277
But if you study and become wise,

11:03.277 --> 11:08.147
you will know the best course of action
 to take, whatever trouble you're in.

11:08.527 --> 11:10.737
That can never be a bad thing.

11:11.357 --> 11:13.657
That's what studying is?

11:16.697 --> 11:17.817
Uncle!

11:17.817 --> 11:20.177
Sorry for startling you! That was me!

11:21.907 --> 11:25.167
This water bucket is all bent
and won't stack anymore.

11:25.397 --> 11:26.807
It no longer sparks joy.

11:26.807 --> 11:28.647
Go and have it repaired.

11:28.647 --> 11:31.157
I'll see to the cooking.

11:31.157 --> 11:33.177
Why, hello there, Sitara.

11:35.297 --> 11:37.927
If you have questions about anything,
 feel free to ask.

11:37.927 --> 11:39.057
I... I will.

11:39.867 --> 11:44.477
<i>Thus Sitara found herself serving
 in a scholarly household,</i>

11:44.477 --> 11:46.237
<i>while studying hard.</i>

12:54.967 --> 12:56.717
You look so pretty, Mistress!

12:57.027 --> 13:00.337
Thank you. But I must admit, 
I feel quite self-conscious.

13:00.337 --> 13:01.767
Don't be silly.

13:02.347 --> 13:05.377
This is your first day going back
 to the hammam baths after your iddah.

13:05.377 --> 13:09.627
Go freshen up, put on some makeup,
dye your hair and hands with henna,

13:09.627 --> 13:12.607
and chat up a storm with the other wives.

13:12.877 --> 13:14.187
If you insist.

13:15.157 --> 13:17.067
I'll take you with me someday,

13:17.747 --> 13:18.617
Sitara.

13:19.847 --> 13:20.617
Sure.

13:23.197 --> 13:26.137
"And to Allah belongs
all that is in the heavens,

13:26.137 --> 13:28.947
and all that is in the earth."

13:30.297 --> 13:33.567
<i>My recitation is still different
than Uncle's somehow.</i>

13:33.567 --> 13:36.047
<i>I'll have him teach me again.</i>

13:36.047 --> 13:37.757
Mother, can we talk?

13:38.537 --> 13:40.007
Uh, where is Mother?

13:40.007 --> 13:43.127
Mistress Fatima went to the hammam.

13:43.617 --> 13:44.887
Didn't she tell you?

13:44.887 --> 13:47.557
What? Oh, was that today?

13:47.557 --> 13:50.497
Is there no room up there
for anything but your studies?

13:51.027 --> 13:54.987
As I've told you, please don't leave
 your room with your hair uncovered.

13:54.987 --> 13:58.137
And as I've told you, I'm still little.

13:58.497 --> 14:01.367
Besides, you're still only 12,
Young Master Muhammad.

14:01.677 --> 14:04.747
What's so bad about someone
who still can't grow a beard

14:04.747 --> 14:06.327
setting foot in a woman's room?

14:06.517 --> 14:08.267
I'm not a child!

14:09.147 --> 14:11.657
Am I immature in your eyes too?

14:17.647 --> 14:21.427
My teacher told me I was too ignorant
 in the ways of the world.

14:21.427 --> 14:23.597
Your law teacher?

14:23.597 --> 14:28.387
Yes, Ustad Kamal al-Din. Father
introduced me to him before he died.

14:29.067 --> 14:32.887
But lately, there are times when I sense
 we view things differently.

14:33.457 --> 14:37.027
He does not even give clear answers
to questions I put to him.

14:37.027 --> 14:42.077
You have far too little experience
to understand such things.

14:43.717 --> 14:46.867
I... intend to go on a journey.

14:48.017 --> 14:51.747
I wish to travel to Nishapur
and visit its renowned teachers.

14:51.747 --> 14:55.587
And I won't stop there.
I will eventually visit other cities

14:55.587 --> 14:57.557
and engage with wisdom

14:57.557 --> 14:59.757
from any and all sources, not just Islam,

15:00.097 --> 15:01.737
in search of truth.

15:06.347 --> 15:10.817
I believe that to be the path my father,
a scholar himself, wanted for me.

15:15.327 --> 15:16.967
That is so admirable.

15:16.967 --> 15:20.067
Well, I have washing to do,
 so I should go.

15:20.067 --> 15:20.947
Sure.

15:24.067 --> 15:28.667
"And to Allah belongs all that is in the
 heavens, and all that is in the earth."

15:32.427 --> 15:35.017
<i>No matter how hard I study,</i>

15:35.017 --> 15:37.837
<i>I'll never match Master Muhammad, will I?</i>

15:53.287 --> 15:55.267
Well, Mother, I'm off.

15:55.267 --> 15:59.617
Devote yourself to your studies there
so as not to bring shame on your father.

15:59.617 --> 16:00.317
I will.

16:00.837 --> 16:03.027
Take good care of yourself.

16:06.387 --> 16:07.877
Well, I'm off.

16:09.017 --> 16:10.517
I'll see you partway there.

16:10.517 --> 16:12.037
Thank you, Uncle.

16:14.287 --> 16:15.627
Wait a moment.

16:15.627 --> 16:16.417
Girl.

16:17.877 --> 16:19.917
I'm told you are still unable to read.

16:20.147 --> 16:21.247
Yes.

16:21.247 --> 16:22.147
I see.

16:22.587 --> 16:24.187
I shall write letters to you.

16:24.677 --> 16:26.877
When I become a teacher in the future,

16:26.877 --> 16:29.507
I'll need to convey lessons
to young children like you.

16:29.507 --> 16:31.617
So I will write as simply as I can.

16:31.617 --> 16:33.267
I'm your way of <i>practicing</i>?

16:33.267 --> 16:36.937
I ask you to study hard
so you can read them to my mother.

16:36.937 --> 16:38.657
Understood, Sitara?

16:40.027 --> 16:42.367
Never stop learning, okay?

16:42.367 --> 16:43.927
I understand. I won't.

16:44.987 --> 16:46.197
I'll be off now.

16:52.477 --> 16:57.747
<i>Muhammad, a boy of Tus who would go on 
to become a scholar of some renown,</i>

16:57.747 --> 17:00.497
<i>and Sitara, a slave girl.</i>

17:01.147 --> 17:05.457
<i>This would be the last time they would 
ever see each other face-to-face.</i>

17:07.447 --> 17:10.387
<b>8 Years Later</b>

17:10.387 --> 17:14.017
"In the name of Allah,
the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful."

17:14.317 --> 17:14.927
Huh?

17:18.387 --> 17:20.147
It's the Tus militia.

17:20.147 --> 17:21.617
Ms. Zumurrud?

17:21.617 --> 17:24.357
They must be off to scout around
 outside the city.

17:24.717 --> 17:28.947
Apparently, armed nomads
have been seen in the area.

17:29.987 --> 17:33.187
My little brother is among them somewhere.

17:33.187 --> 17:34.987
I haven't seen him in ages, though.

17:34.987 --> 17:36.197
Oh?

17:36.197 --> 17:39.817
Mikhail and I were born
in a land far to the west.

17:39.817 --> 17:41.347
One right by the sea.

17:41.347 --> 17:45.257
When the evening sun set,
 everything turned a lovely purple color.

17:45.257 --> 17:46.527
The sea?

17:46.527 --> 17:48.217
We were poor,

17:48.217 --> 17:50.577
but how I loved watching the sea.

17:51.067 --> 17:52.097
Sitara?

17:52.907 --> 17:54.807
Might I trouble you to read this letter?

17:54.807 --> 17:56.567
Yes! Right away!

17:57.037 --> 17:58.727
In the usual room, yes?

17:58.727 --> 18:00.977
My goodness, look how happy she is.

18:03.297 --> 18:03.977
Here goes.

18:04.817 --> 18:06.587
"Mother. Uncle."

18:06.587 --> 18:10.437
"In the eight years since I left,
I have studied many fields of learning,

18:10.437 --> 18:13.697
such as philosophy, mathematics,
medicine, and astronomy."

18:13.697 --> 18:18.057
<i>Nishapur is a large city
where noted scholars gather.</i>

18:18.057 --> 18:20.887
<i>For example, I was instructed 
by Fadl al-Din Damad</i>

18:20.887 --> 18:24.567
<i>in the medical arts founded by Ibn Sina.</i>

18:25.027 --> 18:28.767
<i>Unlike theology, in which 
you simply parrot what you are taught,</i>

18:28.767 --> 18:32.587
<i>science is knowledge built upon 
real-world experience gained by scholars.</i>

18:33.067 --> 18:36.537
<i>I find this manner of learning
far more agreeable.</i>

18:36.537 --> 18:37.577
"And also..."

18:38.887 --> 18:42.297
"If our little star, Sitara,
will deign to listen,

18:42.297 --> 18:47.067
please tell her about Euclid and Ptolemy."

18:49.897 --> 18:51.257
Come with me.

18:58.747 --> 19:01.807
Thank you for showing me
all these precious books.

19:01.807 --> 19:06.847
Think nothing of it. Seeking knowledge
 is the duty of every Muslim.

19:07.217 --> 19:09.927
That's what my late 
scholarly husband told me.

19:10.247 --> 19:12.837
Euclid's <i>Elements</i> is that one there.

19:13.157 --> 19:13.977
Sure.

19:22.467 --> 19:24.907
"A point is that which has no part."

19:24.907 --> 19:27.127
"A line is breadthless length."

19:27.127 --> 19:29.877
"The ends of a line are points."

19:29.877 --> 19:33.757
It's like he's stating obvious things
in an overblown way.

19:33.757 --> 19:36.497
But what makes "obvious things" obvious?

19:36.497 --> 19:41.057
It is by amassing examples one by one
that we prove universal principles.

19:41.877 --> 19:42.957
Was that too hard?

19:42.957 --> 19:47.297
Yes, sorry. I just don't see how 
I can apply this knowledge.

19:47.567 --> 19:50.257
In that case, let's find
a more interesting one for you.

19:50.777 --> 19:54.297
Al-Biruni's <i>Book of Instructions 
in the Elements of the Art of Astrology</i>.

19:54.297 --> 19:55.797
A book on astrology?

19:56.027 --> 19:57.397
More down to earth, right?

19:57.757 --> 19:59.627
Look at this.

20:00.817 --> 20:06.277
"The diameter of the Earth
is 2,163 and 1/3 farsakh,

20:06.277 --> 20:09.277
and its circumference is 6,800 farsakh."

20:09.767 --> 20:12.637
This person traveled
to the ends of the Earth?

20:12.637 --> 20:15.157
Of course not. That's impossible.

20:16.217 --> 20:18.757
By forming a right triangle
using a spot on the ground,

20:18.757 --> 20:22.137
a mountaintop,
 and the center of the Earth,

20:22.137 --> 20:24.857
it is possible to determine 
the Earth's radius.

20:24.857 --> 20:26.417
A mountaintop?

20:27.987 --> 20:33.247
You can also calculate the Earth's 
circumference using the angle of shadows.

20:33.247 --> 20:34.577
Using shadows?

20:39.357 --> 20:43.557
All of this was derived from 
the universal knowledge found in <i>Elements</i>.

20:43.987 --> 20:46.017
Well? Does it pique your interest?

20:47.717 --> 20:48.827
It's burning!

20:48.827 --> 20:49.227
Huh?

20:54.857 --> 20:57.677
It's been one failure after another
with you lately.

20:58.637 --> 21:00.657
I'm sorry, Ms. Anis.

21:01.727 --> 21:03.327
Listen, Sitara.

21:03.327 --> 21:05.367
Slaves do all sorts of jobs.

21:05.627 --> 21:10.157
Some slaves are given an education
in order to entertain their master.

21:10.977 --> 21:14.837
We sometimes even receive
a pledge to be set free.

21:15.207 --> 21:18.937
You shouldn't get your hopes up
too high, though.

21:18.937 --> 21:21.787
We don't get to decide such things.

21:22.267 --> 21:24.387
We aren't people. We're property.

21:24.387 --> 21:25.937
Girls, please...

21:25.937 --> 21:27.347
Gather around.

21:27.907 --> 21:29.647
Can you also go fetch Zumurrud?

21:29.887 --> 21:31.267
What's the matter?

21:31.717 --> 21:35.027
The Tus militia has been defeated
by the nomads.

21:38.987 --> 21:43.287
<i>Heaven did not answer our prayers
 with mercy, but with fire.</i>

21:43.817 --> 21:48.007
<i>Instead of rain, fire embers fell 
across the land, followed by silence,</i>

21:49.177 --> 21:51.417
<i>which took the place of the flames.</i>

21:55.107 --> 21:57.797
<i>Highness, as you can see, we have put down</i>

21:58.067 --> 22:00.067
<i>the fools who took up arms against us.</i>

22:00.407 --> 22:02.027
<i>We will enter their city within days.</i>

22:02.617 --> 22:03.327
<i>Ah...</i>

22:04.237 --> 22:07.077
<i>Speaking of which,
 are there scholars in Tus?</i>

22:07.407 --> 22:08.077
<i>Highness?</i>

22:08.747 --> 22:10.707
<i>I'm looking for something, you see.</i>

23:43.107 --> 23:48.257
<b>The Roses That Bloom in Safar</b>

23:43.597 --> 23:46.287
<i>Next time: "The Roses 
That Bloom in Safar."</i>
